// The balance constraint of a shielded transfer: the values entering equal the values
// leaving plus the fee. Proven in zero knowledge, it lets a chain accept a transfer
// without learning any amount, only that value was conserved. The amounts are inputs
// here; in a full note circuit they are openings of commitments, range proven below.
// Run: zkolang transfer.zkl
input in0;
input in1;
input out0;
input out1;
input fee;

// Zero exactly when the sums balance; the proof exists only for a conserving transfer.
assert (in0 + in1) - (out0 + out1 + fee);

output out0 + out1;
